# Odoo git guidelines (20.0)

Follow https://www.odoo.com/documentation/20.0/contributing/development/git_guidelines.html

When creating commits for Odoo modules, **override generic commit style** with this format.

## Message structure

```
[TAG] module: short imperative header (<= ~50 chars)

Why this change (rationale). Prefer WHY over WHAT.
WHAT only if technical choices need explaining.

task-123
Fixes #123
Closes #123
opw-123
```

Header must read as a sentence after: `if applied, this commit will <header>`.

## Tags (use exactly one)

| Tag | Use |
|-----|-----|
| `[FIX]` | Bug fix |
| `[IMP]` | Improvement / incremental feature work |
| `[ADD]` | New module |
| `[REM]` | Remove dead code / views / modules |
| `[REF]` | Heavy rewrite / refactor |
| `[MOV]` | Move files or code (use `git mv`; no content change in same commit) |
| `[REV]` | Revert |
| `[PERF]` | Performance |
| `[CLN]` | Cleanup |
| `[LINT]` | Linting |
| `[I18N]` | Translations |
| `[MERGE]` | Merge / forward-port umbrella |
| `[REL]` | Release |
| `[CLA]` | CLA |

## Module name

- Use **technical** module name after the tag (`ci_ai`, not a display label).
- One module per commit when practical; if cross-cutting use `various` or list modules.
- Do **not** mix unrelated modules in one commit (eases revert/history).

## Examples

```
[IMP] ci_ai: support OpenAI-compatible gateway presets

Allow DeepSeek/Groq/OpenRouter via allowlisted hosts so admins can BYO
cheaper chat backends without a new adapter per vendor.
```

```
[FIX] ci_ai: reject embeddings on chat-only gateways

Closes #42
```

```
[MOV] ci_ai: split openai gateways into openai_gateways.py
```

## Hygiene

- Do not change git `user.name` / `user.email` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Use `.gitmessage` in this repo as the template when committing locally.
